  "name": "mina-stealth-fixes",
  "description": "An implementation of the Mina Protocol, a layer-1 blockchain that utilizes recursive zero-knowledge proofs to maintain a constant-size chain regardless of transaction volume. The system integrates a core OCaml consensus engine with a Rust-based cryptographic backend and a TypeScript SDK for privacy-preserving smart contracts. It features a decentralized peer-to-peer network layer using libp2p and automated infrastructure for large-scale testnet orchestration.",
